xnu 0470: map the worker's windows on the boot thread

Measured 2026-11-26: with 0468/0469 in, the wifi worker stops at
`W4 BAR map done` on every boot, inside the first `wifi_ahb_page()` -- an
`ml_io_map()` -- while `wifistat` reads the same BAR from the command thread
without trouble. `ml_io_map()` is serialized, so a worker that maps while the
battery thread or the boot block maps blocks in it.

The BAR and the four AHB pages are now mapped by `mondrian_wifi_premap()` from
the boot probe block, before the SPMI key thread and before the worker exists;
`wifi_map_once()` and `wifi_ahb_page()` then return the cached windows inside
the worker. Each step logs its virtual address, so a block names the page.
diff --git a/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c b/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
